# Party banter on Yester Hill. Each node opens with an `if` gate.

~ banter_humming
if not flag.yester_hill_resolved and name:ratatoille and name:thistle
interject name:ratatoille: Listen. One note, held for days, by people taking turns. A ritual of attrition. Fascinating. Horrible, but fascinating.
interject name:thistle: Thirty of them, maybe more. I can smell them from here. Wet wool and bad teeth.
interject name:ratatoille: Thirty. Wonderful. I have revised my position to simply horrible.
endif
-> END

~ banter_effigy
if flag.yester_hill_known and not flag.yester_hill_resolved
interject tag:cheerful: A forty-foot statue of the man in the castle, made of mud. Does he know? Do you think he's flattered?
interject tag:pious: Men like him are always flattered. That's the weak joint in them.
endif
-> END

~ banter_after_the_hill
if flag.yester_hill_resolved and not flag.gulthias_tree_burned
interject tag:blunt: We left the tree.
interject tag:scholarly: Trees don't walk. Generally.
interject tag:blunt: Generally.
endif
-> END

~ banter_burned
if flag.gulthias_tree_burned and name:kip_smudgewick and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:kip_smudgewick: I keep hearing it. The noise it made when it caught. Trees aren't meant to make a noise like that.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Then I'll pray for the next soul who would have climbed that hill, and will never know to thank us.
endif
-> END

~ banter_elvir
if flag.elvir_truth_known and not flag.martikovs_reconciled and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: "I told him fly." The lad sent his brother away and stayed to face them. Sir Pellam would call that a knight's death.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Then his father hears it. Today. Some news you don't leave sitting in a pocket.
endif
-> END
